WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.920
At this point, you've started a project,

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.900
but if you wanna work
with others in Basecamp,

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:04.965
you need to invite them in.

00:00:04.965 --> 00:00:07.170
In this video, I'm gonna
show you how to do it.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.490
So let's say I'm on this project

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.710
and I want to invite someone to it.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.800
At the top left, I'm gonna
hit that people icon,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.870
and you'll see on the left side everyone

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.090
who already has access to this project.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.820
And then I can invite
more people on the right.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.740
So if I start to type someone's name

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.360
and they're already in
my Basecamp account,

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.210
maybe they're on a different
project, their name will pop up

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:29.730
and I can just click it to
add them to this project.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.440
If you're inviting someone
for the first time,

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.060
you'll add their email address.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.350
You can add multiple
people at the same time,

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.750
and you can even customize
the welcome message

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.920
that we email out.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.810
From here, you'll click Send Invites

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.490
and Basecamp emails them

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.680
to let them know they've
been added to a project.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.450
Now, when someone's
added for the first time,

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.330
they're automatically added
as an outside collaborator.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.820
That means they can't
start projects of their own

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.130
or invite new people to a project.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.330
But if you wanna change that

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.950
and make them part of your company

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.360
and give them those permissions,

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:06.000
they can start projects
from scratch, add others,

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.470
and even become administrators,

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.110
you'll just change that
selection right here

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.060
and click save changes.

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:14.550
It's that easy. Now, let's
say you wanna add someone

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.910
to multiple projects all at
the same time. That's easy too.

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.890
So head to your home screen

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:22.590
and click Invite People to the account.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.210
Here you'll have three options

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:26.340
to choose from, someone from your company,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.450
an outside collaborator,

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.610
again, they won't be able to
start new projects on their

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.080
own, or a client.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.290
Now, if you're choosing a
client, you'll be able to turn on

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:37.020
or off access to different
parts of the project.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.540
For this example, let's say
I'm going to work with an

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.240
outside collaborator,
like a vendor partner.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.910
I'll hit next, and then
I'm gonna enter their name,

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.310
their email address, their title.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.200
I'll just call her a vendor,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.750
and then the name of their company.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.530
You can add additional
people with the plus button,

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.970
and again, you can personalize

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:02.550
that note in the invitation
email if you'd like to.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.090
You'll click email invitation now,

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.800
and Basecamp sends them an email

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.470
to set up a password into your account.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.820
Now at this point, you're gonna want

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.820
to set up which projects
this person can see.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.620
So I have all my list of projects,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:20.880
and let's say I want this
person, Leslie, to be added

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.260
to these accounts.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.790
I will save changes.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.040
And now Leslie has access to all

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.200
of those projects all at the same time.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.120
One thing to keep in mind
when you're adding someone

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.520
to an existing project,
they'll have access

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.590
to the complete project history.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.270
It's a great way to catch someone up

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.370
and help them quickly get up to speed,

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.350
but they'll also have access to everything

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.840
that was posted in that
project before they join.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.040
So keep that in mind.

